== Toolset ==
*Listed incorrectly in the [[Toolset]] as a [[Two-handed axe blueprint category|two-handed axe]].

== Sentinel +1 ==
This weapon bears the mark of the dwarf [[Marrok]], Master Blacksmith of [[Neverwinter]]'s Shining Knight Arms and Armor. He forged it early in 1373 DR, to aid the heroes who sought to free his quarantined city from the virulent grasp of the so-called [[Wailing Death]].

*[[Enhancement bonus]]: +1
*[[Light]]: (low, white)
*[[Skill]] bonus: +2 ([[listen]], [[spot]])
*[[Item level restriction|Required level]]: 6

== Sentinel +3 ==
This weapon bears the mark of the dwarf [[Barun Silverblade|Barun]], a Master Blacksmith who worked from a makeshift forge in the Uthgardt village of Beorunna's Well. He forged it late in 1373 DR, to aid the war effort against [[Aribeth|Lady Aribeth the Betrayer]], who was then marching against the northern city of Neverwinter and the Lords' Alliance.

*[[Cast spell]]: [[true seeing]] ([[caster level]] 9, once per [[day]])
*Enhancement bonus: +2
*Light: (low, white)
*Skill bonus: +4 (listen, spot)
*Required level: 16

== Sentinel +8 ==
When the heroes of Neverwinter became famous, the dwarven smith of Neverwinter crafted a special axe in honor of their deeds. During the crafting of this weapon, a fever consumed the smith and drove him to work such magical forces as he had never crafted before. Afterwards he claimed that a god had come upon him and blessed his work.  Mysteriously, the weapon disappeared while on display in the Halls of Justice and has never been seen again.

*Cast spell: true seeing (caster level 9, twice per day)
*Enhancement bonus: +8
*Light: (low, white)
*Skill bonus: +6 (listen, spot)
*Required level: 23